---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Parts Relay workshops | Parts Relay"
  description="Choose a practical worksheet for a service desk enquiry, a distributor callback or the next shift’s handover."
>
  <div class="workshop">
    <div class="workshop-cover">
      <img src="/assets/workshop-traces.svg" alt="" />
      <div class="workshop-emblem">
        <img src="/assets/symbol.svg" alt="" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="workshop-bound">
      <header class="workshop-header">
        <h1 tabindex="-1">Parts Relay workshops</h1>
        <p>
          Bring a repair order, a supplier callback or an unfinished enquiry. Each workshop gives
          you a worksheet you can keep with the job.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="workshop-directory">
        <section>
          <h2>Choose a workshop</h2>
          <p class="workshop-chooser">
            Choose the job you have in front of you. Allow 10 to 15 minutes to work through it.
          </p>
          <div class="workshop-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter workshops by audience">
            <button type="button" data-workshop-filter="All" aria-pressed="true">
              All
            </button>
            <button type="button" data-workshop-filter="Repair shops" aria-pressed="false">
              Repair shops
            </button>
            <button type="button" data-workshop-filter="Distributors" aria-pressed="false">
              Distributors
            </button>
            <button type="button" data-workshop-filter="Both teams" aria-pressed="false">
              Both teams
            </button>
          </div>
          <ul class="workshop-list">
            <li data-workshop-role="Repair shops">
              <span class="workshop-duration">
                <strong>10</strong> min
              </span>
              <a href="/workshops/first-request/">
                <div>
                  <span>Repair shops</span>
                  <h3>From repair order to counter</h3>
                  <p>
                    Turn a technician’s diagnosis into a description the distributor can quote.
                    Start with the position and quantity.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <img src="/assets/workshop.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" />
              </a>
            </li>
            <li data-workshop-role="Distributors">
              <span class="workshop-duration">
                <strong>15</strong> min
              </span>
              <a href="/workshops/fit-check/">
                <div>
                  <span>Distributors</span>
                  <h3>Taking down a worn part number</h3>
                  <p>
                    Use a supplier callback to settle a missing character, a connector question or
                    an incomplete reference.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <img src="/assets/alternator.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
              </a>
            </li>
            <li data-workshop-role="Both teams">
              <span class="workshop-duration">
                <strong>12</strong> min
              </span>
              <a href="/workshops/handoff/">
                <div>
                  <span>Both teams</span>
                  <h3>A handover the next shift can use</h3>
                  <p>
                    Write the note that lets a colleague make the next call without starting the
                    enquiry again.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <img src="/assets/counter.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" />
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="workshop-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </section>
        <aside class="workshop-aside">
          <h2>Working with a colleague?</h2>
          <p>
            Have the person who missed the call read the completed worksheet. Ask which item they
            would price and which detail they would check first.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you picture different parts, find the word that caused the mix-up. “Housing” and
            “complete assembly” can mean different orders at the counter.
          </p>
          <a href="/guides/guidebook/">Read the getting-started guide</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <section class="workshop-debrief">
        <h2>Keep the note with the repair</h2>
        <div>
          <p>
            When a supplier calls back after a shift change, the repair order is usually easier to
            find than the person who took the original call. File the worksheet with that order.
          </p>
          <p>
            Date the latest reply. If the supplier changes the quoted reference, keep the earlier
            number with a short note explaining which one the shop is now considering.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/workshops.js';
</script>
